            "review_title": "Review at Cafe Hoang",
            "review_text": "leah\nMandaluyong, Philippines700 contributions\n0\negg coffee!\nJul 2019\nWe had lunch here as part of a group tour so wasn't really expecting much.\n\nMost of the food were really good, esp. the veggie ones. Then there was egg coffee! Was curios about it so ordered one. The owner taught us how to \"drink\" it which was a novelty. It was really sweet and creamy and delish! And since I don't really like coffee because of its bitter sweet, Hoang's sweet egg coffee was just right for me.\n\nTypical of Hanoi buildings, this cafe is built narrow. We filled the second floor of around 8 tables of four 4 pax each. A small balcony offered a direct view of the street below and the nearby equally narrow buildings - very cute in pictures.\n\nMust be a family business since there were a couple of really young boys helping to serve the food. Worth a second visit - if only to try some of the other dishes - and have that egg coffee again!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 2, 2019",
